{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JFRnuVzxz276PeKkytW1Ze","type":"tool_result","content":"commit af521ed196f2e8b7fe1e4596a9e557243be136aa\nAuthor: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>\nDate:   Mon Apr 13 12:01:28 2026 +0200\n\n    Batch MLE main_ptrs upload: replace per-trace to_device() with single batched upload\n    \n    Replace ~5600 per-trace main_ptrs.to_device() calls in MLE sumcheck rounds\n    with 2 batched uploads per round (one for late_eval Case A traces, one for\n    early_eval Case B traces). Each TraceCtx now holds a raw pointer into a\n    shared DeviceBuffer instead of owning an individual allocation.\n    \n    Changes:\n    - TraceCtx.main_ptrs_dev: DeviceBuffer -> main_ptrs_ptr: *const MainMatrixPtrs\n    - evaluate_mle_constraints_gpu/evaluate_mle_interactions_gpu take raw ptr\n    - sumcheck_polys_batch_eval collects main_ptrs into flat vectors, uploads\n      once, backfills pointers into TraceCtx entries\n    - All batch builder consumers updated to use raw pointer directly\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WFWjUeJtR4i6PboGBx31jh","session_id":"d2e39847-b30b-4a34-8468-d493bf69eac0","uuid":"cc5c737a-bf01-442d-91dc-71f9f3d53bab","timestamp":"2026-04-14T00:44:30.977Z"}
