 improved Round 0 by 1.89x and GKR input eval by 1.40x — should reduce this to ~8ms wall time, saving ~37ms at APC 300.","+Pre-compute the logup Round 0 interaction evaluation DAG, rules, and weight-index mapping at keygen time, eliminating per-AIR `SymbolicConstraints::from()`, `SymbolicDagBuilder` construction, `SymbolicRulesGpu::new()`, rule encoding, and `d_rules` device upload in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`. The keygen code already builds this identical DAG (pkey.rs:116-142) but discards everything except `buffer_size`. Keeping the full pre-computed rules and a compact weight mapping table allows the hot path to skip all DAG reconstruction and only compute challenge-dependent weights (~0.2ms per AIR instead of ~1.0ms). At APC 300 with 623 AIRs across 8 round-robin-balanced threads, this eliminates ~0.8ms of CPU overhead per AIR, yielding ~50-80ms wall-time improvement for Round 0."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-14-0140-multistream-stacked-reduction-round0\n\nMulti-stream the per-trace sequential loops in Stacked Reduction's Round 0 sumcheck (`batch_sumcheck_uni_round0_poly`) and PLE fold (`fold_ple_evals`). These two functions currently launch ~797 sequential per-trace CUDA kernels on the default stream (22ms block_sum + 8ms final_reduce + 9ms fold_ple = 39ms GPU time, ~45ms wall time including launch overhead). Distributing across 8 OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams — the same pattern that improved Round 0 by 1.89x and GKR input eval by 1.40x — should reduce this to ~8ms wall time, saving ~37ms at APC 300.\n"}}
