{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0163DwCCdubQQ5iDGJif9Pxp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Pre-compute logup Round 0 interaction rules at keygen time\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate per-AIR CPU overhead in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` by pre-computing the logup interaction DAG, encoded rules, and weight-index mapping at keygen time. This mirrors the existing pattern where zerocheck constraint rules are pre-computed as `pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0`.\n6\t\n7\tCurrently, each call to `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` (called per AIR per segment — 1246 times at APC 300) rebuilds:\n8\t1. `SymbolicConstraints::from()` — converts DAG back to expression trees (~0.3-0.5ms)\n9\t2. `SymbolicDagBuilder` + `SymbolicExpressionDag` construction (~0.2-0.3ms)\n10\t3. `SymbolicRulesGpu::new()` + rule encoding (~0.1-0.2ms)\n11\t4. `d_rules.to_device()` H2D upload (~0.05ms)\n12\t\n13\tThe keygen code at `pkey.rs:116-142` already builds this identical DAG but discards everything except `buffer_size`. We extend it to keep the full rules and a weight mapping.\n14\t\n15\t## Current Code Path\n16\t\n17\t### Keygen (pkey.rs:89-152)\n18\t\n19\t`AirDataGpu::new()` calls:\n20\t1. `SymbolicConstraints::from(dag)` — converts `SymbolicConstraintsDag` to `SymbolicConstraints` (line 94)\n21\t2. `InteractionEvalRules::new()` — builds GKR input eval rules (line 95)\n22\t3. `ConstraintOnlyRules::<true>::new()` — builds zerocheck Round 0 rules (line 96)\n23\t4. `ConstraintOnlyRules::<false>::new()` — builds zerocheck MLE rules (line 97)\n24\t5. Lines 116-142: Builds the logup round0 interaction DAG (same DAG as `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`), extracts `rules.buffer_size`, discards the rest\n25\t\n26\t### Round 0 hot path (logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:152-319)\n27\t\n28\t`process_air_round0()` calls:\n29\t1. Line 157: `SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints)` — **redundant DAG→tree→DAG roundtrip**\n30\t2. Line 175: `main_parts.to_device()` — H2D of pointer array (~5 pointers)\n31\t3. Lines 197-212: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` — uses pre-computed `pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0` (already optimized)\n32\t4. Lines 262-279: `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` — receives `&single_air_constraints`, rebuilds DAG from scratch\n33\t\n34\t### evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu (round0.rs:162-320)\n35\t\n36\tLines 193-239 (per-AIR overhead, inside block scope):\n37\t1. Lines 194-211: `SymbolicDagBuilder::new()` + iterate interactions + `add_expr()` per count/message field + sort + dedup + build `SymbolicExpressionDag`\n38\t2. Line 213: `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)`\n39\t3. Lines 214-235: Compute `numer_weights[rule_idx]` and `denom_weights[rule_idx]` using `eq_3bs` and `beta_pows` — challenge-dependent, varies per proof\n40\t4. Lines 236-237: `d_numer_weights = numer_weights.to_device()`, `d_denom_weights = denom_weights.to_device()`\n41\t5. Lines 241-242: `encoded_rules.to_device()` → `d_rules`\n42\t\n43\tSteps 1-2 and 5 are invariant (same result for any proof of the same AIR). Step 3-4 depend on prover challenges.\n44\t\n45\tLines 244-320: Buffer allocation, kernel launch, result copy — these remain unchanged.\n46\t\n47\t## Changes\n48\t\n49\t### 1. Add `LogupRound0Rules` struct to `pkey.rs`\n50\t\n51\t```rust\n52\t/// Pre-computed logup Round 0 interaction evaluation rules.\n53\t/// Stores the encoded rules on device and a compact weight mapping\n54\t/// so the hot path only needs to compute challenge-dependent weights.\n55\tpub struct LogupRound0Rules {\n56\t    pub(crate) inner: EvalRules,\n57\t    /// For each interaction: (count_rule_idx, Vec<message_rule_idx>)\n58\t    /// Used to compute numer_weights and denom_weights from eq_3bs/beta_pows.\n59\t    pub(crate) weight_map: Vec<InteractionWeightEntry>,\n60\t    /// Pre-computed denom_sum coefficients: (bus_index, message_len) per interaction\n61\t    pub(crate) denom_sum_entries: Vec<DenomSumEntry>,\n62\t    /// Number of rules (length of numer_weights/denom_weights arrays)\n63\t    pub(crate) num_rules: usize,\n64\t}\n65\t\n66\t/// Maps one interaction to its rule indices for weight computation.\n67\tpub struct InteractionWeightEntry {\n68\t    pub count_rule_idx: usize,\n69\t    pub message_rule_indices: Vec<usize>,\n70\t}\n71\t\n72\t/// Per-interaction data needed for denom_sum_init computation.\n73\tpub struct DenomSumEntry {\n74\t    pub bus_index: u32,\n75\t    pub message_len: usize,\n76\t}\n77\t```\n78\t\n79\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n80\t\n81\t### 2. Modify `AirDataGpu::new()` to build `LogupRound0Rules`\n82\t\n83\tReplace lines 116-142 of `pkey.rs` (the current `logup_round0_buffer_size` computation) with full pre-computation:\n84\t\n85\t```rust\n86\tlet logup_round0 = if !symbolic_constraints.interactions.is_empty() {\n87\t    let mut dag_builder = SymbolicDagBuilder::new();\n88\t    let mut sorted_used_dag_idxs = Vec::new();\n89\t    for interaction in &symbolic_constraints.interactions {\n90\t        let count = dag_builder.add_expr(&interaction.count);\n91\t        sorted_used_dag_idxs.push(count);\n92\t        sorted_used_dag_idxs.extend(\n93\t            interaction.message.iter()\n94\t                .map(|field_expr| dag_builder.add_expr(field_expr)),\n95\t        );\n96\t    }\n97\t    sorted_used_dag_idxs.sort();\n98\t    sorted_used_dag_idxs.dedup();\n99\t    let dag = SymbolicExpressionDag {\n100\t        nodes: dag_builder.nodes,\n101\t        constraint_idx: sorted_used_dag_idxs,\n102\t    };\n103\t    let rules = SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true);\n104\t\n105\t    // Build weight mapping: interaction_idx -> rule indices\n106\t    let weight_map: Vec<InteractionWeightEntry> = symbolic_constraints.interactions.iter()\n107\t        .map(|interaction| {\n108\t            let count_dag_idx = dag_builder.expr_to_idx\n109\t                [&(&interaction.count as *const SymbolicExpression<_>)];\n110\t            let count_rule_idx = rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&count_dag_idx];\n111\t            let message_rule_indices: Vec<usize> = interaction.message.iter()\n112\t                .map(|msg| {\n113\t                    let msg_dag_idx = dag_builder.expr_to_idx\n114\t                        [&(msg as *const SymbolicExpression<_>)];\n115\t                    rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&msg_dag_idx]\n116\t                })\n117\t                .collect();\n118\t            InteractionWeightEntry { count_rule_idx, message_rule_indices }\n119\t        })\n120\t        .collect();\n121\t\n122\t    let denom_sum_entries: Vec<DenomSumEntry> = symbolic_constraints.interactions.iter()\n123\t        .map(|interaction| DenomSumEntry {\n124\t            bus_index: interaction.bus_index as u32,\n125\t            message_len: interaction.message.len(),\n126\t        })\n127\t        .collect();\n128\t\n129\t    let num_rules = rules.rules.len();\n130\t    let encoded_rules = rules.rules.iter().map(|c| c.encode()).collect_vec();\n131\t    let d_rules = encoded_rules.to_device()?;\n132\t    // logup round0 doesn't use used_nodes (see round0.rs:207 comment)\n133\t    let d_used_nodes = DeviceBuffer::new();\n134\t\n135\t    Some(LogupRound0Rules {\n136\t        inner: EvalRules {\n137\t            d_rules,\n138\t            d_used_nodes,\n139\t            buffer_size: rules.buffer_size.try_into().expect(\"buffer_size exceeds u32\"),\n140\t        },\n141\t        weight_map,\n142\t        denom_sum_entries,\n143\t        num_rules,\n144\t    })\n145\t} else {\n146\t    None\n147\t};\n148\t```\n149\t\n150\tUpdate `AirDataGpu` struct to replace `logup_round0_buffer_size: u32` with `logup_round0: Option<LogupRound0Rules>`.\n151\t\n152\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n153\t\n154\t### 3. Update `logup_round0_buffer_size` references\n155\t\n156\tAll existing references to `pk.other_data.logup_round0_buffer_size` (used in Round 0 work item buffer size pre-computation, `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`) must use `pk.other_data.logup_round0.as_ref().map_or(0, |r| r.inner.buffer_size)` instead.\n157\t\n158\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` — search for `logup_round0_buffer_size` and update.\n159\t\n160\t### 4. Refactor `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` to use pre-computed rules\n161\t\n162\tReplace the function signature and body (round0.rs:162-320):\n163\t\n164\t**New signature**:\n165\t```rust\n166\tpub fn evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n167\t    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n168\t    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n169\t    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n170\t    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n171\t    eq_cube: *const EF,\n172\t    beta_pows: &[EF],\n173\t    eq_3bs: &[EF],\n174\t    skip_domain: u32,\n175\t    num_x: u32,\n176\t    height: u32,\n177\t    num_cosets: u32,\n178\t    g_shift: F,\n179\t    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n180\t    prealloc_intermediates: Option<&mut DeviceBuffer<F>>,\n181\t    prealloc_temp_sums: Option<&mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>>,\n182\t) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, Round0EvalError>\n183\t```\n184\t\n185\tRemove the `symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints<F>` parameter. Instead use `pk.other_data.logup_round0`.\n186\t\n187\t**New body** (lines 193-239 replaced with):\n188\t```rust\n189\tif eq_3bs.is_empty() {\n190\t    return Ok(DeviceBuffer::new());\n191\t}\n192\tlet logup_r0 = pk.other_data.logup_round0.as_ref()\n193\t    .expect(\"logup_round0 rules missing for AIR with interactions\");\n194\t\n195\tlet buffer_size = logup_r0.inner.buffer_size;\n196\tlet d_rules = &logup_r0.inner.d_rules;\n197\t\n198\t// Compute challenge-dependent weights using pre-computed mapping\n199\tlet mut numer_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; logup_r0.num_rules];\n200\tlet mut denom_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; logup_r0.num_rules];\n201\tlet mut denom_sum_init = EF::ZERO;\n202\t\n203\tfor (interaction_idx, (entry, denom_entry)) in logup_r0.weight_map.iter()\n204\t    .zip(logup_r0.denom_sum_entries.iter())\n205\t    .enumerate()\n206\t{\n207\t    numer_weights[entry.count_rule_idx] += eq_3bs[interaction_idx];\n208\t    denom_sum_init += eq_3bs[interaction_idx]\n209\t        * beta_pows[denom_entry.message_len]\n210\t        * F::from_u32(denom_entry.bus_index + 1);\n211\t    for (message_idx, &rule_idx) in entry.message_rule_indices.iter().enumerate() {\n212\t        denom_weights[rule_idx] += eq_3bs[interaction_idx] * beta_pows[message_idx];\n213\t    }\n214\t}\n215\tlet d_numer_weights = numer_weights.to_device()?;\n216\tlet d_denom_weights = denom_weights.to_device()?;\n217\t\n218\t// ... rest of function unchanged (buffer allocation, kernel launch, result copy)\n219\t// Uses d_rules from logup_r0 instead of locally constructed d_rules\n220\t```\n221\t\n222\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n223\t\n224\t### 5. Remove `SymbolicConstraints::from()` from `process_air_round0`\n225\t\n226\tIn `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:152-319`, remove:\n227\t- Line 157: `let single_air_constraints = SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints);`\n228\t- Line 264: Remove `&single_air_constraints` parameter from `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` call\n229\t\n230\tThe `single_air_constraints` local is ONLY used as a parameter to `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`. With the pre-computed rules, this is no longer needed.\n231\t\n232\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n233\t\n234\t### 6. Update the kernel launch in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n235\t\n236\tThe kernel launch at round0.rs:295-320 currently uses the locally constructed `d_rules`. After the refactor, it uses `logup_r0.inner.d_rules` from the pre-computed data. Specifically:\n237\t\n238\t```rust\n239\tunsafe {\n240\t    logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0(\n241\t        temp_sums_buffer,\n242\t        &mut s_evals,\n243\t        selectors_cube,\n244\t        preprocessed_ptr,\n245\t        main_parts,\n246\t        eq_cube,\n247\t        &d_numer_weights,  // still per-proof, computed above\n248\t        &d_denom_weights,  // still per-proof, computed above\n249\t        d_rules,           // now from logup_r0.inner.d_rules (pre-computed)\n250\t        buffer_size,\n251\t        intermediates,\n252\t        denom_sum_init,\n253\t        skip_domain,\n254\t        num_x,\n255\t        height,\n256\t        num_cosets,\n257\t        g_shift,\n258\t        max_temp_bytes,\n259\t    )?;\n260\t}\n261\t```\n262\t\n263\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n264\t\n265\t## Invariants\n266\t\n267\t1. **Correctness**: The pre-computed rules produce identical `d_rules` and weight mappings as the current per-call construction. The DAG builder is deterministic given the same symbolic constraints, and the keygen code already builds the exact same DAG (pkey.rs:117-135). The weight computation logic is unchanged — only the mapping from interaction→rule_idx is pre-computed.\n268\t\n269\t2. **Existing zerocheck path unchanged**: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` already uses `pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0` and is not modified.\n270\t\n271\t3. **GKR input eval path unchanged**: `process_gkr_input_air` in gkr_input.rs uses `pk.other_data.interaction_rules` which is a different DAG construction (for the GKR input evaluation, not Round 0). These are distinct DAGs with different topological orderings and buffering strategies.\n272\t\n273\t4. **Fallback for AIRs without interactions**: When `eq_3bs.is_empty()` or `logup_round0` is `None`, return empty buffer immediately (matches current behavior).\n274\t\n275\t5. **Keygen determinism**: The pre-computation uses the same `SymbolicDagBuilder` → `SymbolicRulesGpu::new()` path as the current runtime code. The `expr_to_idx` pointer-based mapping in `SymbolicDagBuilder` is stable because the `symbolic_constraints` lifetime spans the entire keygen call.\n276\t\n277\t6. **Memory**: The pre-computed `LogupRound0Rules` stores `d_rules` (on device, one buffer per AIR), `weight_map` (host-side, compact), and `denom_sum_entries` (host-side, compact). For 623 AIRs, the additional device memory is negligible (each AIR's rules are typically <1KB). Host memory for weight_map is ~10 entries × 623 AIRs = ~50KB.\n278\t\n279\t## Measurement Plan\n280\t\n281\t1. Build the binary in the powdr repo:\n282\t   ```bash\n283\t   cd /home/georg/powdr && cargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"\n284\t   ```\n285\t\n286\t2. Run APC 300 benchmark (3 runs for median):\n287\t   ```bash\n288\t   cd /home/georg/powdr/results/pairing\n289\t   RUST_LOG=info ./target/release/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc300/metrics.json --recursion\n290\t   ```\n291\t   Analyze with `python3 /home/georg/spec.py after_apc300/metrics.json after_apc300`\n292\t\n293\t3. Run APC 0 benchmark to verify no regression:\n294\t   ```bash\n295\t   RUST_LOG=info ./target/release/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n296\t   ```\n297\t\n298\t4. Compare Round 0 time: expect 50-80ms improvement at APC 300, ≤25ms improvement at APC 0.\n299\t5. Compare STARK excl trace: expect 50-80ms improvement at APC 300.\n300\t\n301\t## Rollback Criteria\n302\t\n303\t- Round 0 improvement at APC 300 is less than 25ms (below noise floor).\n304\t- Any regression in STARK excl trace at APC 0 exceeding 20ms.\n305\t- Any regression in other phases (LogUp GKR, MLE Rounds, Openings) exceeding 15ms at any APC configuration.\n306\t- Proof verification fails.\n307\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2e39847-b30b-4a34-8468-d493bf69eac0","uuid":"68b3206e-6715-4f30-8153-87c03ad2981f","timestamp":"2026-04-14T01:05:22.544Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0300-precompute-logup-round0-interaction-rules/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Pre-compute logup Round 0 interaction rules at keygen time\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate per-AIR CPU overhead in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` by pre-computing the logup interaction DAG, encoded rules, and weight-index mapping at keygen time. This mirrors the existing pattern where zerocheck constraint rules are pre-computed as `pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0`.\n\nCurrently, each call to `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` (called per AIR per segment — 1246 times at APC 300) rebuilds:\n1. `SymbolicConstraints::from()` — converts DAG back to expression trees (~0.3-0.5ms)\n2. `SymbolicDagBuilder` + `SymbolicExpressionDag` construction (~0.2-0.3ms)\n3. `SymbolicRulesGpu::new()` + rule encoding (~0.1-0.2ms)\n4. `d_rules.to_device()` H2D upload (~0.05ms)\n\nThe keygen code at `pkey.rs:116-142` already builds this identical DAG but discards everything except `buffer_size`. We extend it to keep the full rules and a weight mapping.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Keygen (pkey.rs:89-152)\n\n`AirDataGpu::new()` calls:\n1. `SymbolicConstraints::from(dag)` — converts `SymbolicConstraintsDag` to `SymbolicConstraints` (line 94)\n2. `InteractionEvalRules::new()` — builds GKR input eval rules (line 95)\n3. `ConstraintOnlyRules::<true>::new()` — builds zerocheck Round 0 rules (line 96)\n4. `ConstraintOnlyRules::<false>::new()` — builds zerocheck MLE rules (line 97)\n5. Lines 116-142: Builds the logup round0 interaction DAG (same DAG as `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`), extracts `rules.buffer_size`, discards the rest\n\n### Round 0 hot path (logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:152-319)\n\n`process_air_round0()` calls:\n1. Line 157: `SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints)` — **redundant DAG→tree→DAG roundtrip**\n2. Line 175: `main_parts.to_device()` — H2D of pointer array (~5 pointers)\n3. Lines 197-212: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` — uses pre-computed `pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0` (already optimized)\n4. Lines 262-279: `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` — receives `&single_air_constraints`, rebuilds DAG from scratch\n\n### evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu (round0.rs:162-320)\n\nLines 193-239 (per-AIR overhead, inside block scope):\n1. Lines 194-211: `SymbolicDagBuilder::new()` + iterate interactions + `add_expr()` per count/message field + sort + dedup + build `SymbolicExpressionDag`\n2. Line 213: `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)`\n3. Lines 214-235: Compute `numer_weights[rule_idx]` and `denom_weights[rule_idx]` using `eq_3bs` and `beta_pows` — challenge-dependent, varies per proof\n4. Lines 236-237: `d_numer_weights = numer_weights.to_device()`, `d_denom_weights = denom_weights.to_device()`\n5. Lines 241-242: `encoded_rules.to_device()` → `d_rules`\n\nSteps 1-2 and 5 are invariant (same result for any proof of the same AIR). Step 3-4 depend on prover challenges.\n\nLines 244-320: Buffer allocation, kernel launch, result copy — these remain unchanged.\n\n## Changes\n\n### 1. Add `LogupRound0Rules` struct to `pkey.rs`\n\n```rust\n/// Pre-computed logup Round 0 interaction evaluation rules.\n/// Stores the encoded rules on device and a compact weight mapping\n/// so the hot path only needs to compute challenge-dependent weights.\npub struct LogupRound0Rules {\n    pub(crate) inner: EvalRules,\n    /// For each interaction: (count_rule_idx, Vec<message_rule_idx>)\n    /// Used to compute numer_weights and denom_weights from eq_3bs/beta_pows.\n    pub(crate) weight_map: Vec<InteractionWeightEntry>,\n    /// Pre-computed denom_sum coefficients: (bus_index, message_len) per interaction\n    pub(crate) denom_sum_entries: Vec<DenomSumEntry>,\n    /// Number of rules (length of numer_weights/denom_weights arrays)\n    pub(crate) num_rules: usize,\n}\n\n/// Maps one interaction to its rule indices for weight computation.\npub struct InteractionWeightEntry {\n    pub count_rule_idx: usize,\n    pub message_rule_indices: Vec<usize>,\n}\n\n/// Per-interaction data needed for denom_sum_init computation.\npub struct DenomSumEntry {\n    pub bus_index: u32,\n    pub message_len: usize,\n}\n```\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n\n### 2. Modify `AirDataGpu::new()` to build `LogupRound0Rules`\n\nReplace lines 116-142 of `pkey.rs` (the current `logup_round0_buffer_size` computation) with full pre-computation:\n\n```rust\nlet logup_round0 = if !symbolic_constraints.interactions.is_empty() {\n    let mut dag_builder = SymbolicDagBuilder::new();\n    let mut sorted_used_dag_idxs = Vec::new();\n    for interaction in &symbolic_constraints.interactions {\n        let count = dag_builder.add_expr(&interaction.count);\n        sorted_used_dag_idxs.push(count);\n        sorted_used_dag_idxs.extend(\n            interaction.message.iter()\n                .map(|field_expr| dag_builder.add_expr(field_expr)),\n        );\n    }\n    sorted_used_dag_idxs.sort();\n    sorted_used_dag_idxs.dedup();\n    let dag = SymbolicExpressionDag {\n        nodes: dag_builder.nodes,\n        constraint_idx: sorted_used_dag_idxs,\n    };\n    let rules = SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true);\n\n    // Build weight mapping: interaction_idx -> rule indices\n    let weight_map: Vec<InteractionWeightEntry> = symbolic_constraints.interactions.iter()\n        .map(|interaction| {\n            let count_dag_idx = dag_builder.expr_to_idx\n                [&(&interaction.count as *const SymbolicExpression<_>)];\n            let count_rule_idx = rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&count_dag_idx];\n            let message_rule_indices: Vec<usize> = interaction.message.iter()\n                .map(|msg| {\n                    let msg_dag_idx = dag_builder.expr_to_idx\n                        [&(msg as *const SymbolicExpression<_>)];\n                    rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&msg_dag_idx]\n                })\n                .collect();\n            InteractionWeightEntry { count_rule_idx, message_rule_indices }\n        })\n        .collect();\n\n    let denom_sum_entries: Vec<DenomSumEntry> = symbolic_constraints.interactions.iter()\n        .map(|interaction| DenomSumEntry {\n            bus_index: interaction.bus_index as u32,\n            message_len: interaction.message.len(),\n        })\n        .collect();\n\n    let num_rules = rules.rules.len();\n    let encoded_rules = rules.rules.iter().map(|c| c.encode()).collect_vec();\n    let d_rules = encoded_rules.to_device()?;\n    // logup round0 doesn't use used_nodes (see round0.rs:207 comment)\n    let d_used_nodes = DeviceBuffer::new();\n\n    Some(LogupRound0Rules {\n        inner: EvalRules {\n            d_rules,\n            d_used_nodes,\n            buffer_size: rules.buffer_size.try_into().expect(\"buffer_size exceeds u32\"),\n        },\n        weight_map,\n        denom_sum_entries,\n        num_rules,\n    })\n} else {\n    None\n};\n```\n\nUpdate `AirDataGpu` struct to replace `logup_round0_buffer_size: u32` with `logup_round0: Option<LogupRound0Rules>`.\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n\n### 3. Update `logup_round0_buffer_size` references\n\nAll existing references to `pk.other_data.logup_round0_buffer_size` (used in Round 0 work item buffer size pre-computation, `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`) must use `pk.other_data.logup_round0.as_ref().map_or(0, |r| r.inner.buffer_size)` instead.\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` — search for `logup_round0_buffer_size` and update.\n\n### 4. Refactor `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` to use pre-computed rules\n\nReplace the function signature and body (round0.rs:162-320):\n\n**New signature**:\n```rust\npub fn evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    eq_cube: *const EF,\n    beta_pows: &[EF],\n    eq_3bs: &[EF],\n    skip_domain: u32,\n    num_x: u32,\n    height: u32,\n    num_cosets: u32,\n    g_shift: F,\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n    prealloc_intermediates: Option<&mut DeviceBuffer<F>>,\n    prealloc_temp_sums: Option<&mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>>,\n) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, Round0EvalError>\n```\n\nRemove the `symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints<F>` parameter. Instead use `pk.other_data.logup_round0`.\n\n**New body** (lines 193-239 replaced with):\n```rust\nif eq_3bs.is_empty() {\n    return Ok(DeviceBuffer::new());\n}\nlet logup_r0 = pk.other_data.logup_round0.as_ref()\n    .expect(\"logup_round0 rules missing for AIR with interactions\");\n\nlet buffer_size = logup_r0.inner.buffer_size;\nlet d_rules = &logup_r0.inner.d_rules;\n\n// Compute challenge-dependent weights using pre-computed mapping\nlet mut numer_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; logup_r0.num_rules];\nlet mut denom_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; logup_r0.num_rules];\nlet mut denom_sum_init = EF::ZERO;\n\nfor (interaction_idx, (entry, denom_entry)) in logup_r0.weight_map.iter()\n    .zip(logup_r0.denom_sum_entries.iter())\n    .enumerate()\n{\n    numer_weights[entry.count_rule_idx] += eq_3bs[interaction_idx];\n    denom_sum_init += eq_3bs[interaction_idx]\n        * beta_pows[denom_entry.message_len]\n        * F::from_u32(denom_entry.bus_index + 1);\n    for (message_idx, &rule_idx) in entry.message_rule_indices.iter().enumerate() {\n        denom_weights[rule_idx] += eq_3bs[interaction_idx] * beta_pows[message_idx];\n    }\n}\nlet d_numer_weights = numer_weights.to_device()?;\nlet d_denom_weights = denom_weights.to_device()?;\n\n// ... rest of function unchanged (buffer allocation, kernel launch, result copy)\n// Uses d_rules from logup_r0 instead of locally constructed d_rules\n```\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\n### 5. Remove `SymbolicConstraints::from()` from `process_air_round0`\n\nIn `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:152-319`, remove:\n- Line 157: `let single_air_constraints = SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints);`\n- Line 264: Remove `&single_air_constraints` parameter from `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` call\n\nThe `single_air_constraints` local is ONLY used as a parameter to `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`. With the pre-computed rules, this is no longer needed.\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\n### 6. Update the kernel launch in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n\nThe kernel launch at round0.rs:295-320 currently uses the locally constructed `d_rules`. After the refactor, it uses `logup_r0.inner.d_rules` from the pre-computed data. Specifically:\n\n```rust\nunsafe {\n    logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0(\n        temp_sums_buffer,\n        &mut s_evals,\n        selectors_cube,\n        preprocessed_ptr,\n        main_parts,\n        eq_cube,\n        &d_numer_weights,  // still per-proof, computed above\n        &d_denom_weights,  // still per-proof, computed above\n        d_rules,           // now from logup_r0.inner.d_rules (pre-computed)\n        buffer_size,\n        intermediates,\n        denom_sum_init,\n        skip_domain,\n        num_x,\n        height,\n        num_cosets,\n        g_shift,\n        max_temp_bytes,\n    )?;\n}\n```\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: The pre-computed rules produce identical `d_rules` and weight mappings as the current per-call construction. The DAG builder is deterministic given the same symbolic constraints, and the keygen code already builds the exact same DAG (pkey.rs:117-135). The weight computation logic is unchanged — only the mapping from interaction→rule_idx is pre-computed.\n\n2. **Existing zerocheck path unchanged**: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` already uses `pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0` and is not modified.\n\n3. **GKR input eval path unchanged**: `process_gkr_input_air` in gkr_input.rs uses `pk.other_data.interaction_rules` which is a different DAG construction (for the GKR input evaluation, not Round 0). These are distinct DAGs with different topological orderings and buffering strategies.\n\n4. **Fallback for AIRs without interactions**: When `eq_3bs.is_empty()` or `logup_round0` is `None`, return empty buffer immediately (matches current behavior).\n\n5. **Keygen determinism**: The pre-computation uses the same `SymbolicDagBuilder` → `SymbolicRulesGpu::new()` path as the current runtime code. The `expr_to_idx` pointer-based mapping in `SymbolicDagBuilder` is stable because the `symbolic_constraints` lifetime spans the entire keygen call.\n\n6. **Memory**: The pre-computed `LogupRound0Rules` stores `d_rules` (on device, one buffer per AIR), `weight_map` (host-side, compact), and `denom_sum_entries` (host-side, compact). For 623 AIRs, the additional device memory is negligible (each AIR's rules are typically <1KB). Host memory for weight_map is ~10 entries × 623 AIRs = ~50KB.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Build the binary in the powdr repo:\n   ```bash\n   cd /home/georg/powdr && cargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"\n   ```\n\n2. Run APC 300 benchmark (3 runs for median):\n   ```bash\n   cd /home/georg/powdr/results/pairing\n   RUST_LOG=info ./target/release/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc300/metrics.json --recursion\n   ```\n   Analyze with `python3 /home/georg/spec.py after_apc300/metrics.json after_apc300`\n\n3. Run APC 0 benchmark to verify no regression:\n   ```bash\n   RUST_LOG=info ./target/release/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n   ```\n\n4. Compare Round 0 time: expect 50-80ms improvement at APC 300, ≤25ms improvement at APC 0.\n5. Compare STARK excl trace: expect 50-80ms improvement at APC 300.\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Round 0 improvement at APC 300 is less than 25ms (below noise floor).\n- Any regression in STARK excl trace at APC 0 exceeding 20ms.\n- Any regression in other phases (LogUp GKR, MLE Rounds, Openings) exceeding 15ms at any APC configuration.\n- Proof verification fails.\n","numLines":307,"startLine":1,"totalLines":307}}}
