{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AoRbm5RktS75y6HDTBG8T8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Pre-compute logup Round 0 interaction rules at keygen time\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate per-AIR CPU overhead in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` by pre-computing the logup interaction DAG, encoded rules, and weight-index mapping at keygen time. This mirrors the existing pattern where zerocheck constraint rules are pre-computed as `pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0`.\n6\t\n7\tCurrently, each call to `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` (called per AIR per segment — 1246 times at APC 300) rebuilds:\n8\t1. `SymbolicConstraints::from()` — converts DAG back to expression trees (~0.3-0.5ms)\n9\t2. `SymbolicDagBuilder` + `SymbolicExpressionDag` construction (~0.2-0.3ms)\n10\t3. `SymbolicRulesGpu::new()` + rule encoding (~0.1-0.2ms)\n11\t4. `d_rules.to_device()` H2D upload (~0.05ms)\n12\t\n13\tThe keygen code at `pkey.rs:116-142` already builds this identical DAG but discards everything except `buffer_size`. We extend it to keep the full rules and a weight mapping.\n14\t\n15\t## Current Code Path\n16\t\n17\t### Keygen (pkey.rs:89-152)\n18\t\n19\t`AirDataGpu::new()` calls:\n20\t1. `SymbolicConstraints::from(dag)` — converts `SymbolicConstraintsDag` to `SymbolicConstraints` (line 94)\n21\t2. `InteractionEvalRules::new()` — builds GKR input eval rules (line 95)\n22\t3. `ConstraintOnlyRules::<true>::new()` — builds zerocheck Round 0 rules (line 96)\n23\t4. `ConstraintOnlyRules::<false>::new()` — builds zerocheck MLE rules (line 97)\n24\t5. Lines 116-142: Builds the logup round0 interaction DAG (same DAG as `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`), extracts `rules.buffer_size`, discards the rest\n25\t\n26\t### Round 0 hot path (logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:152-319)\n27\t\n28\t`process_air_round0()` calls:\n29\t1. Line 157: `SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints)` — **redundant DAG→tree→DAG roundtrip**\n30\t2. Line 175: `main_parts.to_device()` — H2D of pointer array (~5 pointers)\n31\t3. Lines 197-212: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` — uses pre-computed `pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0` (already optimized)\n32\t4. Lines 262-279: `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` — receives `&single_air_constraints`, rebuilds DAG from scratch\n33\t\n34\t### evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu (round0.rs:162-320)\n35\t\n36\tLines 193-239 (per-AIR overhead, inside block scope):\n37\t1. Lines 194-211: `SymbolicDagBuilder::new()` + iterate interactions + `add_expr()` per count/message field + sort + dedup + build `SymbolicExpressionDag`\n38\t2. Line 213: `SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true)`\n39\t3. Lines 214-235: Compute `numer_weights[rule_idx]` and `denom_weights[rule_idx]` using `eq_3bs` and `beta_pows` — challenge-dependent, varies per proof\n40\t4. Lines 236-237: `d_numer_weights = numer_weights.to_device()`, `d_denom_weights = denom_weights.to_device()`\n41\t5. Lines 241-242: `encoded_rules.to_device()` → `d_rules`\n42\t\n43\tSteps 1-2 and 5 are invariant (same result for any proof of the same AIR). Step 3-4 depend on prover challenges.\n44\t\n45\tLines 244-320: Buffer allocation, kernel launch, result copy — these remain unchanged.\n46\t\n47\t## Changes\n48\t\n49\t### 1. Add `LogupRound0Rules` struct to `pkey.rs`\n50\t\n51\t```rust\n52\t/// Pre-computed logup Round 0 interaction evaluation rules.\n53\t/// Stores the encoded rules on device and a compact weight mapping\n54\t/// so the hot path only needs to compute challenge-dependent weights.\n55\tpub struct LogupRound0Rules {\n56\t    pub(crate) inner: EvalRules,\n57\t    /// For each interaction: (count_rule_idx, message_rule_indices).\n58\t    /// Used to compute numer_weights and denom_weights from eq_3bs/beta_pows\n59\t    /// without rebuilding the DAG.\n60\t    pub(crate) weight_map: Vec<InteractionWeightEntry>,\n61\t    /// Number of rules (length of numer_weights/denom_weights arrays)\n62\t    pub(crate) num_rules: usize,\n63\t}\n64\t\n65\t/// Maps one interaction to its rule indices for weight computation.\n66\tpub struct InteractionWeightEntry {\n67\t    pub count_rule_idx: usize,\n68\t    pub message_rule_indices: Vec<usize>,\n69\t    /// Bus index for this interaction (copied from VK at keygen time).\n70\t    pub bus_index: u32,\n71\t}\n72\t```\n73\t\n74\tNote: `bus_index` and `message_len` (= `message_rule_indices.len()`) are stored directly in `InteractionWeightEntry` rather than in a separate struct — this avoids a redundant type and avoids re-deriving them from the VK's `DagInteraction` at runtime (which would require a separate DAG→interaction lookup).\n75\t\n76\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n77\t\n78\t### 2. Modify `AirDataGpu::new()` to build `LogupRound0Rules`\n79\t\n80\tReplace lines 116-142 of `pkey.rs` (the current `logup_round0_buffer_size` computation) with full pre-computation:\n81\t\n82\t```rust\n83\tlet logup_round0 = if !symbolic_constraints.interactions.is_empty() {\n84\t    let mut dag_builder = SymbolicDagBuilder::new();\n85\t    let mut sorted_used_dag_idxs = Vec::new();\n86\t    for interaction in &symbolic_constraints.interactions {\n87\t        let count = dag_builder.add_expr(&interaction.count);\n88\t        sorted_used_dag_idxs.push(count);\n89\t        sorted_used_dag_idxs.extend(\n90\t            interaction.message.iter()\n91\t                .map(|field_expr| dag_builder.add_expr(field_expr)),\n92\t        );\n93\t    }\n94\t    sorted_used_dag_idxs.sort();\n95\t    sorted_used_dag_idxs.dedup();\n96\t    let dag = SymbolicExpressionDag {\n97\t        nodes: dag_builder.nodes,\n98\t        constraint_idx: sorted_used_dag_idxs,\n99\t    };\n100\t    let rules = SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true);\n101\t\n102\t    // Build weight mapping: interaction_idx -> rule indices\n103\t    let weight_map: Vec<InteractionWeightEntry> = symbolic_constraints.interactions.iter()\n104\t        .map(|interaction| {\n105\t            let count_dag_idx = dag_builder.expr_to_idx\n106\t                [&(&interaction.count as *const SymbolicExpression<_>)];\n107\t            let count_rule_idx = rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&count_dag_idx];\n108\t            let message_rule_indices: Vec<usize> = interaction.message.iter()\n109\t                .map(|msg| {\n110\t                    let msg_dag_idx = dag_builder.expr_to_idx\n111\t                        [&(msg as *const SymbolicExpression<_>)];\n112\t                    rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&msg_dag_idx]\n113\t                })\n114\t                .collect();\n115\t            InteractionWeightEntry {\n116\t                count_rule_idx,\n117\t                message_rule_indices,\n118\t                bus_index: interaction.bus_index as u32,\n119\t            }\n120\t        })\n121\t        .collect();\n122\t\n123\t    let num_rules = rules.rules.len();\n124\t    let encoded_rules = rules.rules.iter().map(|c| c.encode()).collect_vec();\n125\t    let d_rules = encoded_rules.to_device()?;\n126\t    // logup round0 doesn't use used_nodes (see round0.rs:207 comment)\n127\t    let d_used_nodes = DeviceBuffer::new();\n128\t\n129\t    Some(LogupRound0Rules {\n130\t        inner: EvalRules {\n131\t            d_rules,\n132\t            d_used_nodes,\n133\t            buffer_size: rules.buffer_size.try_into().expect(\"buffer_size exceeds u32\"),\n134\t        },\n135\t        weight_map,\n136\t        num_rules,\n137\t    })\n138\t} else {\n139\t    None\n140\t};\n141\t```\n142\t\n143\tUpdate `AirDataGpu` struct to replace `logup_round0_buffer_size: u32` with `logup_round0: Option<LogupRound0Rules>`.\n144\t\n145\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n146\t\n147\t### 3. Update `logup_round0_buffer_size` references\n148\t\n149\tAll existing references to `pk.other_data.logup_round0_buffer_size` (used in Round 0 work item buffer size pre-computation, `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`) must use `pk.other_data.logup_round0.as_ref().map_or(0, |r| r.inner.buffer_size)` instead.\n150\t\n151\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` — search for `logup_round0_buffer_size` and update.\n152\t\n153\t### 4. Refactor `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` to use pre-computed rules\n154\t\n155\tReplace the function signature and body (round0.rs:162-320):\n156\t\n157\t**New signature**:\n158\t```rust\n159\tpub fn evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n160\t    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n161\t    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n162\t    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n163\t    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n164\t    eq_cube: *const EF,\n165\t    beta_pows: &[EF],\n166\t    eq_3bs: &[EF],\n167\t    skip_domain: u32,\n168\t    num_x: u32,\n169\t    height: u32,\n170\t    num_cosets: u32,\n171\t    g_shift: F,\n172\t    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n173\t    prealloc_intermediates: Option<&mut DeviceBuffer<F>>,\n174\t    prealloc_temp_sums: Option<&mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>>,\n175\t) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, Round0EvalError>\n176\t```\n177\t\n178\tRemove the `symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints<F>` parameter. Instead use `pk.other_data.logup_round0`.\n179\t\n180\t**New body** (lines 193-239 replaced with):\n181\t```rust\n182\tif eq_3bs.is_empty() {\n183\t    return Ok(DeviceBuffer::new());\n184\t}\n185\tlet logup_r0 = pk.other_data.logup_round0.as_ref()\n186\t    .expect(\"logup_round0 rules missing for AIR with interactions\");\n187\t\n188\tlet buffer_size = logup_r0.inner.buffer_size;\n189\tlet d_rules = &logup_r0.inner.d_rules;\n190\t\n191\t// Compute challenge-dependent weights using pre-computed mapping\n192\tlet mut numer_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; logup_r0.num_rules];\n193\tlet mut denom_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; logup_r0.num_rules];\n194\tlet mut denom_sum_init = EF::ZERO;\n195\t\n196\tfor (interaction_idx, entry) in logup_r0.weight_map.iter().enumerate() {\n197\t    numer_weights[entry.count_rule_idx] += eq_3bs[interaction_idx];\n198\t    denom_sum_init += eq_3bs[interaction_idx]\n199\t        * beta_pows[entry.message_rule_indices.len()]\n200\t        * F::from_u32(entry.bus_index + 1);\n201\t    for (message_idx, &rule_idx) in entry.message_rule_indices.iter().enumerate() {\n202\t        denom_weights[rule_idx] += eq_3bs[interaction_idx] * beta_pows[message_idx];\n203\t    }\n204\t}\n205\tlet d_numer_weights = numer_weights.to_device()?;\n206\tlet d_denom_weights = denom_weights.to_device()?;\n207\t\n208\t// ... rest of function unchanged (buffer allocation, kernel launch, result copy)\n209\t// Uses d_rules from logup_r0 instead of locally constructed d_rules\n210\t```\n211\t\n212\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n213\t\n214\t### 5. Remove `SymbolicConstraints::from()` from `process_air_round0`\n215\t\n216\tIn `logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:152-319`, remove:\n217\t- Line 157: `let single_air_constraints = SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints);`\n218\t- Line 264: Remove `&single_air_constraints` parameter from `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` call\n219\t\n220\tThe `single_air_constraints` local is ONLY used as a parameter to `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`. With the pre-computed rules, this is no longer needed.\n221\t\n222\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n223\t\n224\t### 6. Update the kernel launch in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`\n225\t\n226\tThe kernel launch at round0.rs:295-320 currently uses the locally constructed `d_rules`. After the refactor, it uses `logup_r0.inner.d_rules` from the pre-computed data. The only change is the source of `d_rules` and `buffer_size` — all other arguments are unchanged. The existing call site at round0.rs:303 provides the correct argument order matching the FFI signature at `cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs:1015-1034`:\n227\t\n228\t```rust\n229\t// Existing argument order (unchanged, only d_rules source changes):\n230\tlogup_bary_eval_interactions_round0(\n231\t    temp_sums_buffer,        // &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>\n232\t    &mut s_evals,            // &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>\n233\t    selectors_cube,          // &DeviceBuffer<F>\n234\t    preprocessed_ptr,        // *const F\n235\t    main_parts,              // &DeviceBuffer<*const F>\n236\t    eq_cube,                 // *const EF\n237\t    public_values,           // &DeviceBuffer<F>\n238\t    &d_numer_weights,        // &DeviceBuffer<EF> (still per-proof)\n239\t    &d_denom_weights,        // &DeviceBuffer<EF> (still per-proof)\n240\t    denom_sum_init,          // EF (still per-proof)\n241\t    d_rules,                 // &DeviceBuffer<u128> — NOW from logup_r0.inner.d_rules\n242\t    buffer_size,             // u32 — NOW from logup_r0.inner.buffer_size\n243\t    intermediates,           // &mut DeviceBuffer<F>\n244\t    skip_domain,             // u32\n245\t    num_x,                   // u32\n246\t    height,                  // u32\n247\t    num_cosets,              // u32\n248\t    g_shift,                 // F\n249\t    max_temp_bytes,          // usize\n250\t)\n251\t```\n252\t\n253\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n254\t\n255\t## Invariants\n256\t\n257\t1. **Correctness**: The pre-computed rules produce identical `d_rules` and weight mappings as the current per-call construction. The DAG builder is deterministic given the same symbolic constraints, and the keygen code already builds the exact same DAG (pkey.rs:117-135). The weight computation logic is unchanged — only the mapping from interaction→rule_idx is pre-computed.\n258\t\n259\t2. **Existing zerocheck path unchanged**: `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` already uses `pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0` and is not modified.\n260\t\n261\t3. **GKR input eval path unchanged**: `process_gkr_input_air` in gkr_input.rs uses `pk.other_data.interaction_rules` which is a different DAG construction (for the GKR input evaluation, not Round 0). These are distinct DAGs with different topological orderings and buffering strategies.\n262\t\n263\t4. **Fallback for AIRs without interactions**: When `eq_3bs.is_empty()` or `logup_round0` is `None`, return empty buffer immediately (matches current behavior).\n264\t\n265\t5. **Keygen determinism**: The pre-computation uses the same `SymbolicDagBuilder` → `SymbolicRulesGpu::new()` path as the current runtime code. The `expr_to_idx` pointer-based mapping in `SymbolicDagBuilder` is stable because the `symbolic_constraints` local is not moved between the DAG build loop and the weight-map build loop (both occur within the same block in `AirDataGpu::new()`). Note: if future refactoring moves `symbolic_constraints` ownership between these two phases, the `expr_to_idx` pointers would dangle. The current design keeps both phases in the same scope to prevent this.\n266\t\n267\t6. **Memory**: The pre-computed `LogupRound0Rules` stores `d_rules` (on device, one buffer per AIR), `weight_map` (host-side, compact), and `denom_sum_entries` (host-side, compact). For 623 AIRs, the additional device memory is negligible (each AIR's rules are typically <1KB). Host memory for weight_map is ~10 entries × 623 AIRs = ~50KB.\n268\t\n269\t## Measurement Plan\n270\t\n271\t0. **Validate per-AIR overhead estimate** (before full benchmarking): Add a temporary `std::time::Instant` around the eliminated code block (round0.rs:193-239) for a single APC 300 run. Verify the measured per-AIR overhead is ≥0.3ms. If <0.3ms, the total improvement will be below the 25ms rollback threshold and the optimization should be reconsidered.\n272\t\n273\t1. Build the binary in the powdr repo:\n274\t   ```bash\n275\t   cd /home/georg/powdr && cargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"\n276\t   ```\n277\t\n278\t2. Run APC 300 benchmark (3 runs for median):\n279\t   ```bash\n280\t   cd /home/georg/powdr/results/pairing\n281\t   RUST_LOG=info ./target/release/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc300/metrics.json --recursion\n282\t   ```\n283\t   Analyze with `python3 /home/georg/spec.py after_apc300/metrics.json after_apc300`\n284\t\n285\t3. Run APC 0 benchmark to verify no regression:\n286\t   ```bash\n287\t   RUST_LOG=info ./target/release/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc000.cbor --input 0 --metrics after_apc000/metrics.json --recursion\n288\t   ```\n289\t\n290\t4. Compare Round 0 time: expect 50-80ms improvement at APC 300, ≤25ms improvement at APC 0.\n291\t5. Compare STARK excl trace: expect 50-80ms improvement at APC 300.\n292\t\n293\t## Rollback Criteria\n294\t\n295\t- Round 0 improvement at APC 300 is less than 25ms (below noise floor).\n296\t- Any regression in STARK excl trace at APC 0 exceeding 20ms.\n297\t- Any regression in other phases (LogUp GKR, MLE Rounds, Openings) exceeding 15ms at any APC configuration.\n298\t- Proof verification fails.\n299\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016H9H2SzxUJPdjH3bDpsXaB","session_id":"d2e39847-b30b-4a34-8468-d493bf69eac0","uuid":"c4ba50d5-71d4-4322-8600-22d98d9c383d","timestamp":"2026-04-14T01:06:38.844Z"}
